Guidelime.registerGuide([[
[N 25-26 Blackfathom Deeps]
[D Forever Shaman 1-30 (Braedyn)\\The Blackfathom Deeps run from the Zoram Strand: Researching the Corruption, Twilight Falls, In Search of Thaelrid, Blackfathom Villainy and (shaman) Knowledge in the Deeps, with boss notes, loot calls and the hearth home.]
[GA Alliance]
[OC]|cffffffffLevel 25|r  -  you stand on the Zoram Strand in north-west Ashenvale; hearth = Sentinel Hill. This chapter is one dungeon, Blackfathom Deeps: a full clear of 22-28 mobs with bosses at 25-28. Only Thaelrid pays out inside (2,400 XP); the other quests are finished here and handed in later: about 13,400 quest XP in all (about 10,650 for a hunter, who skips Knowledge in the Deeps). Group content: bring the tank friend and a healer, you two are the damage
[OC]|cffffcc00Log check:|r Researching the Corruption (1275, from Auberdine), In Search of Thaelrid (1198) and Twilight Falls (1199) (both from Darnassus), and for the shaman Knowledge in the Deeps (971, from Gerrig). Blackfathom Villainy needs 1198 handed in first, so without 1198 you lose it too
[OC]|cffffcc00Supplies:|r there is no vendor inside, so arrive stocked: food and water for an hour, repair, empty bags, and (hunter) 400+ ammo
[OC]|cffffcc00Sources:|r Forever's Blackfathom is reported to be Classic's dungeon with only the loot changed. Levels, drops, quests and item stats below come from the Forever DB; boss tactics, locations and the brazier event are Classic-era guide knowledge (Icy Veins, Almar's, Forever guides) and not verified on Forever

[OC]|cffffffffBlackfathom Deeps|r  -  |cFFFF0000GROUP 5|r, finder level 15 (Classic figure), mobs 22-28, bosses 25-28, ~60 min. Your quests (only Blackfathom Villainy is picked up inside):
[OC]|cffffcc00?|r Researching the Corruption (1275) - 8 Corrupted Brain Stems - |cff66ff66normal|r: nine mob types in the DB drop it (every Fallenroot satyr, Blackfathom Tide Priestess, Oracle, Sea Witch, Myrmidon and Lady Sarevess), so the cave mouth and the first caverns usually cover it; the drop rate itself is not in the DB. Hands in to Gershala in Auberdine (chapter 20)
[OC]|cffffcc00?|r In Search of Thaelrid (1198) - find Argent Guard Thaelrid in an alcove of Ghamoo-ra's chamber - |cff66ff66normal|r, 2,400 XP on the spot, and he gives Blackfathom Villainy
[OC]|cffffcc00?|r Blackfathom Villainy (1200) - the Head of Kelris - |cff66ff66normal|r, a quest drop from Twilight Lord Kelris; 3,300 XP at Selgorm in Darnassus (chapter 20)
[OC]|cffffcc00?|r Twilight Falls (1199) - 10 Twilight Pendants - |cff66ff66normal|r if you kill every Twilight cultist from the flooded ruins to Kelris (Acolyte, Reaver, Aquamancer, Loreseeker, Shadowmage and Elementalist all drop them; the drop rate is not in the DB, so if you are a few short at the end, go back for the cultists you skipped). 2,550 XP at Manados in Darnassus (chapter 20)
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00?|r Knowledge in the Deeps (971) - the Lorgalis Manuscript from a Pitted Iron Chest - |cff66ff66normal|r, but the chest is underwater; 2,750 XP at Gerrig in Ironforge (chapter 15)
[OC][A Hunter] Knowledge in the Deeps (971) was optional in chapter 08 and is not tracked for hunters: if you picked it up, the chest notes under Ghamoo-ra apply to you and Gerrig takes it whenever you pass Ironforge; if not, skip it
[OC]|cffffcc00Maybe:|r The Heart of the Void (78916, level 25): the DB only knows its end, Selgorm in Darnassus, and its text, "Bring the Blackfathom Pearl". Its giver and the Pearl's source are not in the DB (the three reward items are not in the tooltip service yet either). If a Blackfathom Pearl ever drops, keep it and hand it in at Selgorm with the others; this guide does not track the quest
[OC]|cffffcc00Not for you:|r Baron Aquanis, Amongst the Ruins, Allegiance to the Old Gods, The Essence of Aku'mai and Trouble in the Deeps are Horde quests; Alliance has no sapphire quest

|cFFFF0000GROUP 5|r Gather at the sunken temple on the Zoram Strand and enter Blackfathom Deeps at the cave mouth [G14.5,14.2 Ashenvale]
[OC]|cffffcc00The cave mouth|r is held by elites: Fallenroot Satyrs and Blackfathom Tide Priestesses (level 20-21 in the DB; Forever also lists level-25 versions of both, plus Blackfathom Oracles, in the same spot). Pull them in twos, priestesses (healers) first; each one is already a brain-stem chance
[OC]Classic-era: the way in is a swim through a pool at the foot of the ruins and a winding cave of elite naga; the first cavern inside is crossed on stepping stones over water, and falling in sends you back to the start and usually pulls mobs
[OC][A Hunter] |cffffcc00In a group:|r pet on passive, Growl OFF, send it only at the tank's target. Freezing Trap is your crowd control here (Lady Sarevess' guards are the planned use)

[OC]|cffffffffThe run|r  -  one long sweep: Ghamoo-ra's chamber, Lady Sarevess to the north-west, the south tunnel to Gelihast and Lorgus Jett, the water section with Old Serra'kis, the temple and Twilight Lord Kelris, the braziers, Aku'mai. Several trash mobs disarm the tank (Classic-era): DPS ease off for a few seconds after one. Caster naga and murlocs (Sea Witch, Tide Priestess, Oracle) cast and heal: kill them first and interrupt what you can (shaman Earth Shock)
[OC]|cffffcc00Ghamoo-ra|r (25 elite turtle) in the first big chamber: very high armour, so physical hits do about half damage and the shaman's shocks and Searing Totem do the real work. The tank faces him away from the group; everyone steps out of Trample (random target)
[OC]|cffffcc00Loot (both):|r Spiked Shell Band (ring +5 Sta, thorns, unique) only for an empty ring slot. Tortoise Armor is mail and Ghamoo-ra's Bind is cloth - pass
Once the chamber is clear, in the alcove on its south-west side at [TAR4787 Argent Guard Thaelrid], [QT1198] [QA1200 Blackfathom Villainy]
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00Knowledge in the Deeps:|r the Pitted Iron Chest is underwater on the north side of this chamber (Icy Veins; another guide says an alcove of the same room, so look in the water first). Mind your breath bar: Water Breathing is the Classic shaman spell at level 22 (unverified on Forever), otherwise a potion or elixir. The chest respawns slowly, so loot it before the group moves on
[A Shaman] Dive for the Pitted Iron Chest and loot the Lorgalis Manuscript [QC971]
[OC]|cffffcc00Lady Sarevess|r (25 elite naga) with two naga guards in the cavern north-west of the chamber, a short swim away: the tank takes all three, one guard is held (hunter: Freezing Trap), the other dies first. Forked Lightning is a frontal cone that chains between targets: nobody stacks or stands in front of her. She also casts Slow and Frost Nova, and she drops Corrupted Brain Stems
Keep looting Corrupted Brain Stems - if you are still short here, they keep dropping from every satyr, priestess, sea witch and myrmidon on the way [QC1275]
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00Loot (Sarevess):|r |cff66ff66Naga Battle Gloves|r (leather, +4 Str +4 Sta +5 spell damage, req 22) are a gloves upgrade for most. Darkwater Talwar is a sword and Naga Heartpiercer a bow - pass
[OC][A Hunter] |cffffcc00Loot (Sarevess):|r |cff66ff66Naga Heartpiercer|r (bow 13.3 dps, 42-damage proc that stuns naga, req 22) if it beats your current bow; the Fallenroot Longbow from Lorgus Jett is the other candidate. Gun users pass; the gloves (Str) and the Talwar are not for you
[OC]|cffffcc00Gelihast|r (26 elite murloc, skippable for quests but he drops the shaman's best weapon) at the end of the south tunnel past Ghamoo-ra. The murlocs round him are the real danger: pull one pack at a time, then pull him alone. His Net roots a random player. Click the stone behind him for Blessing of Blackfathom (Classic-era: +5 Int and +5 Spi, a long buff)
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00Loot (Gelihast):|r |cff66ff66Reef Axe|r (2H axe 22.4 dps +8 Str, req 22) - ROLL, about 3 dps over Rockslicer or the Spider Leg staff. Cursed Murloc Eye (trinket, 2 Shadow damage on every spell and hit) only for an empty trinket slot. Algae Fists are mail - pass
[OC][A Hunter] |cffffcc00Loot (Gelihast):|r Cursed Murloc Eye (trinket, 2 Shadow damage on spells and attacks, 8 against murlocs) only for an empty trinket slot. Reef Axe and the mail Algae Fists are not for you
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00Leather helms (req 25, bind on pickup):|r Gelihast, Lorgus Jett, Serra'kis, Kelris and Aku'mai each drop one of several. |cff66ff66Defender's Leather Helm|r (+12 Str +13 Sta) is the call, Totemic (+13 Sta +12 spell damage) second; Brawler's, Stormrider's and Wisdom's are not for you
[OC][A Hunter] |cffffcc00Leather helms (req 25, bind on pickup):|r Gelihast, Lorgus Jett, Kelris and Aku'mai drop them. |cff66ff66Brawler's Leather Helm|r (+10 Agi +13 Sta) is the call; the Str, spell-damage and Spirit helms are not for you
[OC]|cffffcc00Lorgus Jett|r (26 elite, optional): a Horde quest target in the northern tunnel after Gelihast (Classic-era: several possible spawns, so skip him if he is not on your path). Lightning Shield - melee wait or Purge it - and Lightning Bolt on the tank. The Forever DB gives him Twilight Maul, Treacherous Treads and Fallenroot Longbow (one Forever guide lists only the longbow)
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00Loot (Lorgus):|r |cff66ff66Twilight Maul|r (2H mace 22.9 dps, +12 spell damage, 70 Nature damage proc, req 23) is the same tier as Reef Axe: take whichever drops, the Maul if you see both. Treacherous Treads are mail - pass
[OC][A Hunter] |cffffcc00Loot (Lorgus):|r |cff66ff66Fallenroot Longbow|r (bow 13.9 dps +2 Agi +4 Sta, req 23) if it beats your bow. Twilight Maul and the mail Treads are not for you
[OC]|cffffcc00Baron Aquanis|r (28 elite): summoned by clicking the Fathom Stone in the water section past the fork, and only the Horde quest cares. Leave the stone alone - he drops nothing for you
[OC]|cffffcc00Old Serra'kis|r (26 elite thresher, skippable for quests, worth it for the loot): in the swim-only cave beside the Baron's stone under the ruins. The whole fight is underwater, so top up breath first (Water Breathing again) and burn him fast; he heals himself every so often, so save a burst for it
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00Loot (Serra'kis):|r |cff66ff66Bands of Serra'kis|r (leather bracers +6 Str +3 Sta, req 22) unless your bracers are better; |cff66ff66Glowing Thresher Cape|r (+8 Spi, +3 spell damage) for a cloak with fewer stats; Bite of Serra'kis is a dagger - pass
[OC][A Hunter] |cffffcc00Loot (Serra'kis):|r nothing for you (Str bracers, Spirit cloak, a dagger) - pass, or take the Bands only for an empty wrist slot
[OC]|cffffffffThe temple|r  -  above the water the ruins and the temple are full of Twilight cultists (Acolyte, Reaver, Aquamancer, Loreseeker, Shadowmage, Elementalist: level 24-26 elite casters). They are your pendants, so kill every one. Aquamancers are said to summon water elementals (Classic-era): kill the caster first. Pull casters back to the tank and interrupt
Loot Twilight Pendants from the cultists - if you are short, kill the ones you skipped before you start the braziers [QC1199]
[OC]|cffffcc00Twilight Lord Kelris|r (27 elite warlock) in the ceremonial chamber before Aku'mai's door. He pulls the cultists round him into the fight, so clear the room first. Mind Blast hits hard and Sleep takes a player out: a sleeping tank means a second tank or a big threat hit must hold him; dispel the Sleep if you can. Sources disagree on interrupting Mind Blast - try one Earth Shock or kick and see
[OC][A Shaman] Drop a Tremor Totem before the pull, it stops the Sleep (Classic-era)
Kill Twilight Lord Kelris and loot the Head of Kelris [QC1200]
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00Loot (Kelris):|r Rod of the Sleepwalker (2H staff 17.7 dps +11 Spi, 32 spell damage) only if your 2H is weaker than Reef Axe or Maul; it roughly ties Rockslicer. Twilight Lord Girdle is mail and Gaze Dreamer Pants cloth - pass. Helm calls above
[OC][A Hunter] |cffffcc00Loot (Kelris):|r nothing for you (staff, cloth, mail belt) - pass; the Brawler's helm call above still applies
[OC]|cffffcc00The braziers|r (Classic-era: four, round the central statue before Aku'mai's door): click one, kill what it calls (Aku'mai Servants, level 26 elite water elementals in the DB), then light the next. The elementals hit in AoE, so kill one as fast as you can and keep the group together. With all four done the door behind the statue opens
[OC]|cffffcc00Aku'mai|r (28 elite hydra) in the lair behind the statue: Poison Cloud on the ground - the tank pulls him out of it and everyone leaves it at once (it can be interrupted); Frenzied Rage (+75% attack speed for about 5 seconds) - stuns and defensive cooldowns then, he can kill a full-health tank quickly. Shaman: Poison Cleansing Totem if you have the Water Totem, otherwise heal through it
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00Loot (Aku'mai):|r |cff66ff66Moss Cinch|r (leather belt +5 Sta +12 spell damage, req 25) beats the Heartwood Girdle that Twilight Falls gives. Strike of the Hydra is a 2H sword (shamans cannot use it) and Leech Pants are cloth - pass. Helm calls above (Stormrider's drops here only)
[OC][A Hunter] |cffffcc00Loot (Aku'mai):|r Strike of the Hydra (2H sword 25.6 dps, req 26, no stats) only if you trained 2H Swords and want a melee stick; Moss Cinch only for a weak belt; Leech Pants are cloth
[OC]|cffffcc00Trash loot (both):|r |cff66ff66Ring of Precision|r (+6 Agi +3 Spi, bind on equip, unique) is the ring for both of you if the slot is empty or weaker. Onyx Claymore (2H sword +10 Str) is a hunter stat stick at best; Staff of the Blessed Seer and Staff of the Friar are caster staves; Tree Bark Jacket is cloth - pass

[OC]|cffffcc00After Aku'mai:|r click the stone behind him for Blessing of Blackfathom if you want it. Nothing hands in down here (Thaelrid was the only inside hand-in), and the Hearthstone works from inside the instance, so there is no walk out
|cFFfff8a3Hearth to [H Sentinel Hill]|r
[OC]|cffffffffHand-ins that wait|r  -  1275 Researching the Corruption: Gershala on the Auberdine dock, at chapter 20's Auberdine pass (the boat is not on your way home). 1200 and 1199: Selgorm and Manados in Darnassus, also chapter 20. Shaman 971: Gerrig Bonegrip in Ironforge, chapter 15. Keep all of them in the log
[OC]|cffffcc00Training:|r no trainer on this route. If you skipped your level-24 spells, they wait for the next city you pass
[OC]|cffffcc00Check:|r log should hold Researching the Corruption (1275), Twilight Falls (1199), Blackfathom Villainy (1200) and, shaman, Knowledge in the Deeps (971), all four completed and waiting for hand-ins, plus the carries from chapters 09-12 (1024, 4581, 1035, 1070 and 973 in the plan). Next: walk from Sentinel Hill into Duskwood
[NX 25-26 Duskwood: Darkshire]
]], "Forever Shaman 1-30")
